# Which common skills from AIAE-llm-aux to install into both discovery registries.
#
# Hand-edited. This is the *selection*; `.llm-aux-manifest` is the generated
# record of what sync actually installed. Sync only ever deletes skills recorded
# in the manifest, so a project-owned skill can never be removed by accident.
#
# Removing a name here and re-running sync uninstalls that skill.
# One skill name per line. `#` starts a comment.
#
# Exactly one user-facing compliance skill ships: `aiae-rule-compliance-audit`,
# which audits against this template's known layout (CLAUDE.md, .claude/rules,
# .claude/agent_docs). The generic `rule-compliance-audit` in AIAE-llm-aux
# discovers unknown rule layouts — valuable for other consumers, redundant here,
# and its trigger list was word-for-word identical, so no agent could choose
# between them. It stays upstream and is deliberately not selected.

verification-gate
production-code-review
fullstack-performance-audit
task-workflow
